course: dictionary
lesson: 14249
title: Negotiation: reaching agreement
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A negotiation is a talk where people try to reach an agreement when they want different things. «Sam wanted to stay up until nine, but Mum wanted him in bed at eight. They had a negotiation and agreed on half past eight.» Both sides gave a little, so both got something.
explain: The verb is negotiate, which means to talk something through until you agree. «We negotiated over who would walk the dog.» A negotiation needs at least two sides, because you need someone to agree with.
explain: Grown-ups use the word in bigger ways too. «The two countries held peace negotiations for six months.» Negotiations are formal talks, often with teams sitting at tables, and they can take a long time. «After long negotiation, the workers and the company agreed on a pay rise.»
explain: Sometimes the word has a looser meaning: finding a way through something difficult. «She had to negotiate the crowded, muddy path with her heavy bag.» Check the clues: people are talking or working something out. Swap in «talks» or «agreement» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Negotiation means talking with others to reach an agreement.
fact: Negotiations are formal talks between countries, companies or groups.
fact: «Open to negotiation» means willing to talk and change the deal.
fact: «After long negotiation» means after a lot of talking to reach an agreement.
fact: Negotiate is the verb: to talk until you agree.
exercise: «Sam and Mum had a negotiation about bedtime, and they agreed on half past eight.» What does negotiation mean here? | A short, quiet sleep | Having a fight that nobody wins | A bedtime story read aloud | *Talking to reach an agreement
exercise: «The two countries held peace negotiations to end the war.» What are peace negotiations? | A holiday trip taken together | Fighting between two armies | Games played in the school hall | *Formal talks to end a conflict
exercise: Ellie says, «Let's negotiate who uses the computer first.» What does negotiate mean? | Keep the computer for yourself | Argue loudly until someone cries | Throw a coin and never speak again | *Talk together until you both agree
test: «The workers and the company had a long negotiation about pay, and then they agreed a rise.» What does «after long negotiation» tell you? | After a game of football | Because the company lost its money | Quickly, with no talking at all | *After a lot of talking to reach an agreement
test: Jayden sees a sign: «Prices open to negotiation.» What does this mean? | Nobody is allowed to speak in the shop | The shop is closed | Only children can buy things here | *The price might change if you talk about it
exam: Which sentence uses negotiate to mean finding a way through something difficult? | *«She had to negotiate the crowded, muddy path with her heavy bag.» | «We drew a picture of the sea.» | «The bus was late again.»
